# Alternative layout for a runner-only AMD EPYC 4545P host with only 64 GB
# (16 cores / 32 threads): four heavy slots, no xl. The retired 64 GB
# intent-ci3 ran it. Prefer a 128 GB box with the intent-ci1 layout. Copy it,
# set RUNNER_NAME_PREFIX to the host's name, then install with
#   infra/runners/install.sh --config <copy>
# See docs/GITHUB_RUNNERS.md, "Add a runner host". Not secret.
GITHUB_ORG=intent-hq
RUNNER_GROUP=intent-cache
RUNNER_GROUP_REPOS=intent,intentd,cloudlands-fe
RUNNER_NAME_PREFIX=intent-runner-2
RUNNER_POOLS=heavy

# CPU n and n+16 are SMT siblings (Linux numbers every core's first thread,
# then every second thread; install.sh checks thread_siblings_list).

# Heavy pool: four 8-thread slots, two per CCD (cores 0-3, 4-7 on CCD 0;
# 8-11, 12-15 on CCD 1), each with both SMT siblings of its cores. Every core
# is pinned. Memory: 4 x 12 GB = 48 GB, under the 51G runners.slice cap (the
# box reports 60 GiB of its 64 GB, minus 9), leaving about 12 GiB for the
# system and Docker. Too small for intent-cache-bigmem: one rustc in intentd's
# 16-core check passed 12 GB and was OOM-killed on intent-ci3. If 8-core jobs
# are OOM-killed too, drop to three slots (HEAVY_SLOTS=3, HEAVY_MEMORY=16g).
HEAVY_SLOTS=4
HEAVY_LABELS=self-hosted,linux,x64,intent-cache
HEAVY_CPUSETS=0-3,16-19 4-7,20-23 8-11,24-27 12-15,28-31
HEAVY_MEMORY=12g
HEAVY_PIDS=16384
HEAVY_SHM=1g
